<p>
This study aims to examine the interrelationships and dynamics of
BIM-based WLCA challenges to provide net zero policy strategies in different jurisdictions. 

To this end, 20 challenges were first identified
from a literature review. A questionnaire survey was then conducted with 145
international professionals and academics across 23 countries.

Based on the survey responses measured by the 5-point Likert scale, mean scores
and the correlation coefficients were computed for the 20 challenges.

Subsequently, mean score rankings, agreement, correlation, network, and centrality analysis were carried out
to map the interrelationships among the 20 BIM-based WLCA challenges (see Figure 2).
</p>

