<h2>How builtenv-cna works: a strong focus on system interdependency and visualisation, without pre-defined models</h2>

<p>
Correlation network analysis (CNA) investigates the interrelationships among variables based on the Graph Theory.
CNA originates from Social Network Analysis (SNA) to study the interconnectivity of relationships among individuals, 
for example the spread of COVID-19 in societies.

Yet, unlike traditional SNA in sustainable construction, which focuses on stakeholders and organisations,
builtenv-cna focuses on system dynamics among the 20 challenges where:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Challenges are represented as network nodes</li>

<li>Correlations are represented as weighted edges</li>

<li>Network metrics identify influential variables</li>

<li>Community detection reveals hidden structural patterns</li>

<li>Networks can be exported directly to Gephi for visualisation and analysis</li>
</ul>

<p>
Figure 3 shows the correlation network analysis workflow, which first transforms 145 collected numeric questionnaire responses 
into correlation heatmaps.

Afterwards, a threshold value based on the correlation coefficient (r value) was chosen to determine
whether a graphical network relationship exists between each pair of challenges.
In this study, a threshold value of r = 0.30 was adopted with reference to previous literature findings.

According to Cohen's (1988) benchmark, an r value of 0.30 represents a “moderate” relationship.
While a higher threshold, for example r = 0.50, would retain the “strong” relationships and plausibly derive more rigorous research findings.
Nonetheless, such a restrictive selection criterion possibly neglects the weaker but structurally representative associations. 
Excluding these weak connections oversimplifies the network creation and introduces potential statistical biases.

On the other hand, the selection of a threshold value of 0.30 is empirically supported by Gignac and Szodorai (2016)’s meta-analysis of 708 correlation coefficients.

Since this study’s research objective is not about the computational deduction and optimization of threshold value, 
no sensitivity analysis was conducted to determine the best fit.
</p>

