<h2>What do the correlation heatmaps and network graphs reveal?
    Global VS regional pathways to net zero buildings</h2>

<p>
The correlation coefficients were color-coded on the scale of -1 (blue) to 1 (red) and visualized in a symmetrical heatmap. Most of the challenge pairs displayed positive correlations.

In all jurisdictions, the closest correlation was formed with #Challenge 18 “BQ, Drawings and
Specifications are not conforming with the requirements of WLCA”
and #Challenge 20 “lack of sitespecific information to render accurate WLCA calculations”. 

The strongest positive relationships were detected in China, with only one negative correlation between 
#Challenge 01 “Insufficiency of BIM to carry out WLCA at early design stage”
and #Challenge 19 “Intellectual Property and privacy concerns about data-sharing on BIM platforms”.

Meanwhile, China and the USA surprisingly exhibited the closest adoption
challenge archetypes despite their agonistic geopolitical relationships.
</p>

