<section class="framework">

<h2>A research and policy toolkit: 4 fundamental features</h2>

<p class="framework-intro">
builtenv-cna models BIM-based whole life carbon assessment challenges as interconnected systems rather than isolated variables. 
The framework enables researchers, policymakers, and professionals to identify the underlying graphical relationships 
with 4 fundamental features:

</p>

<div class="framework-grid">

<div class="framework-card">
<h3>📊 Correlation Analysis</h3>

<ul>
<li>Pearson</li>
<li>Spearman</li>
<li>Kendall</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="framework-card">
<h3>🕸 Network Creation</h3>

<ul>
<li>Weighted edges</li>
<li>Threshold filtering</li>
<li>Signed networks</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="framework-card">
<h3>📈 Network Analytics</h3>

<ul>
<li>Centrality metrics: degree, betweenness, closeness, eigenvector</li>
<li>Community detection</li>
<li>Network density</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="framework-card">
<h3>🌍 Visualisation</h3>

<ul>
<li>Correlation heatmaps</li>
<li>Network graphs</li>
<li>Gephi export</li>
</ul>
</div>

</div>
